    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class). Build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` feature for pet owners, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field (mapped to column `customer_code`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **Schema files** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres`/schema.sql) \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table. Tests run against HSQLDB with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to exist in `schema.sql`; the others are updated for consistency.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field (MapStruct auto-maps it by name in `OwnerMapper`).\n\n4. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, before saving, the code is generated via a new `generateCustomerCode(lastName)` helper:\n   - `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`\n   - `NNNN` = `findAllOwners().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits (`String.format(\"%s-%04d\", ...)`)\n\nThis gives a global sequence one more than the current owner count (e.g. `SMI-0007`). The `AcceptanceTest` and full suite pass (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).",
